# PDP Versions — **v6 active** (v1–v5 frozen)

Routes on **`main`**: **v1** `/v1` · **v2** `/v2` · **v3** `/v3` · **v4** `/v4` · **v5** `/v5` · **v6** `/v6` ← **only active work surface**.

Docs: `docs/pdp-versions.md` · `docs/deploy-and-links.md` · `docs/rounds/README.md`

## Active work = `/v6` only

- Implement and polish **only** on **v6** (`src/app/v6/`, v6 flags in `pdp-version-config.ts`, v6-scoped CSS).
- Treat **v1–v5 as frozen** — do not change their defaults, routes, or look unless explicitly asked to fix a cross-version bug.
- Share/preview link: `/v6` (see `docs/deploy-and-links.md`).

## Rules

- New work → `src/components/pdp/version/` or flags in `pdp-version-config.ts`. Never rewrite v1–v5 defaults.
- Do not branch on `version === "v2"|"v3"|"v4"|"v5"|"v6"`. Add a flag to `PdpVersionConfig`.
- Never edit `pdp-data.ts` or `pdp-section-chapters.ts` for new-round needs.
- Version-only CSS → `src/app/vN/pdp-vN.css` under `[data-pdp-version="vN"]`, not `globals.css`.
- Shared `pdp-v2-*` / `pdp-v5-*` components may render on later routes — gate **v6-only** layout behind **v6** flags.
- After changes: spot-check `/v1`–`/v5` unchanged, then `pnpm check:versions`.

## Quick map

- `pdp-version-context.tsx` · `pdp-version-config.ts` (`V6_CONFIG`)
- Routes: `src/app/v6/` · CSS: `src/app/v6/pdp-v6.css`
- v2 data/chapters · v3: `pdp-v3-*.tsx` · v4: `pdp-v4-specs.ts` · v5: `pdp-v5-*.tsx`
- Boundaries: `scripts/check-pdp-version-boundaries.mjs`
